Recoverpe - Global CTO Constraints & Rules

Project: Next.js 14 (App Router), Supabase (PostgreSQL), Firebase (Auth/Storage), Tailwind CSS.

1. CSV Upload Constraints (Vercel Serverless Limits)

NEVER attempt to send raw CSV files larger than 4.5MB directly to a Next.js serverless API route. It will crash.

For the CSV Ingestion Engine (Part 6), strictly implement frontend file size validation (Limit: 2MB).

If a file exceeds 2MB, implement a frontend chunking utility (e.g., PapaParse) to parse the file on the client-side and send the JSON payload to the backend in safe batches.

2. Meta WhatsApp API (Development Mode)

Do NOT assume immediate production access to the Meta Cloud API.

Implement a server-only APP_ENV variable.

If APP_ENV=development, all outgoing WhatsApp message functions must BYPASS the actual HTTP POST request to Meta. Instead, they must route the payload to console.log or a custom local UI logger to simulate successful delivery.

3. PDF Generation Strict Constraint

NEVER use Puppeteer, Playwright, or any headless browser for PDF generation. It violates our serverless size constraints.

Strictly use @react-pdf/renderer to generate the Tax Invoices directly from React components into byte streams.

4. UI/UX Strict Guidelines

Strictly adhere to the Bright Mode theme. No dark mode.

Primary: White (#FFFFFF) and Pitch Black (#0A0A0A).

Status: Success Green (#10B981) and Error Red (#EF4444).

Avoid heavy drop shadows. Use 1px solid light grey borders for cards and tables.

5. Security & Authentication

Next.js Route Handlers (/app/api/...) MUST verify the Firebase Auth token or Supabase authenticated session before executing any logic.

Do not trust client-side data for prices, subscriptions, or Vapi credit deductions.